# Set token privately using your HTTP client's environment support.
@origin = http://127.0.0.1:8080
@token = {{$processEnv SAMI_API_KEY}}
### Supported native decision
POST {{origin}}/v1/decisions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"task_id":"service_triage","input":{"message":"Serial 1600 is overheating","asset_id":"asset:unit_84","as_of":"2026-10-02"},"pack_id":"industrial-service"}
### Scoped search
POST {{origin}}/v1/knowledge/search
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"query":"overheating PX320","purpose":"service_prequalification","limit":10}
### Research: inference never grants effect permission
POST {{origin}}/v1/research/dsl.execute
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"program":{"op":"compare","operator":"le","left":{"op":"field","path":"hours"},"right":{"op":"literal","value":2000}},"data":{"hours":800}}
### Audit (next page uses the last returned epoch)
GET {{origin}}/v1/audit?after=0&limit=100
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
